Package: imsd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         iproute2,
         libopencore-amrnb0,
         libopencore-amrwb0,
         libqmi-utils,
         libvo-amrwbenc0,
         modemmanager,
         nftables,
         pipewire-bin,
         polkitd,
Description: userspace IMS/VoLTE daemon for mainline Linux phones
 imsd implements the IMS client (SIP registration over IPsec, calls with
 AMR/AMR-WB media) in userspace for Qualcomm modems that do not run IMS
 themselves on mainline Linux, such as the Fairphone (Gen. 6). It brings up
 the ims PDN through ModemManager, reads the P-CSCF over QMI, installs its
 security associations with `ip xfrm` and plays call audio through PipeWire.
 .
 Dialers reach it on the system bus as net.catcrafts.IMS1; see imsd-ofono
 (GNOME Calls) and imsd-plasma (Plasma Dialer).

Package: imsd-ofono
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imsd (= ${binary:Version}), gnome-calls
Conflicts: ofono
Description: GNOME Calls backend for imsd (Phosh, GNOME Mobile)
 imsd-ofonod presents imsd as an oFono modem on the system bus, the interface
 GNOME Calls' ofono provider drives, and points GNOME Calls at that provider.
 It cannot run alongside a real oFono.

Package: imsd-plasma
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imsd (= ${binary:Version})
Enhances: plasma-dialer
Description: Plasma Dialer backend for imsd (Plasma Mobile)
 imsd-dialerd serves the org.kde.telephony.* session-bus interfaces Plasma
 Dialer consumes, bridging them to imsd, in place of kde-telephony's
 modem daemon.
